      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen Image 2.1 on Raylight\n\n**Models** from [Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1):\n- `diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_bf16.safetensors` (14.2 GB), or `qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors` (7.3 GB)\n- `text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_bf16.safetensors` (17.5 GB), or `qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors` (9.4 GB)\n- `vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors`\n\n---\n\n## Parallelism (Ray Init Actor)\n\n- **USP + FSDP** (this workflow): `ulysses_degree` = number of GPUs, `ring_degree` 1, `FSDP` on. The BF16 model does not fit a 12 GB card by itself; FSDP shards its weights across the GPUs.\n- **Less VRAM**: also turn on `FSDP_CPU_OFFLOAD` (slower), set `weight_dtype` to fp8_e4m3fn in Load Diffusion Model (Ray), or use the int8_convrot file.\n- **CFG parallel**: `cfg_degree` 2 and cfg above 1. The positive and negative must encode to the same length (a zeroed-out negative, for example), otherwise there is nothing to split. Qwen Image 2.1 normally runs at cfg 1.\n- **Data parallel** (one image per GPU): Data Parallel KSampler with a Data Parallel Noise List; `ulysses_degree`, `ring_degree` and `cfg_degree` at 0.\n\nMeasured on 2x RTX 3060 12 GB with these settings (BF16, FSDP + USP, 1024x1024, 20 steps): about 100 s from a cold start including model loading, peaking near 9.3 / 8.5 GB per GPU. With FSDP CPU offload the peak was about 4.8 / 4.2 GB.\n\nThe Qwen Image 2.1 Cache node does not apply: under USP and FSDP, Raylight keeps the prompt prefix cache off and recomputes it every step.\n\n---\n\n### [Raylight on GitHub](https://github.com/komikndr/raylight)\n### [Raylight guide on YouTube](https://youtu.be/KQxrkJAV4eI?si=hAFY1rKD6Y2UHXqY)\n"
      ],
      "title": "Qwen Image 2.1 on Raylight",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        40,
        -320
      ],
      "size": [
        320,
        220
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Set ulysses_degree to the number of GPUs and keep ring_degree at 1.\n\nFSDP is what lets the 14 GB BF16 model run on 12 GB cards. Turn it off if the whole model fits on each card."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
